[00:01.00] <Disgracefully>
[00:11.30] <Some folks grow old gracefully>
[00:17.46] <I seem to have misplaced the instructions>
[00:33.60] <My doctor says I ought to slow down>
[00:36.82] <stop climbing ladders and running around. I nodded politely and shook his hand>
[00:43.70] <then forgot the whole conversation again>
[00:50.64] <My hair turned gray, my back got stiff, but>
[00:56.02] <I still think every bad idea's a gift>
[00:59.70] <I should know better by now>
[01:01.34] <it's true>
[01:02.84] <but knowing better ain't what I always do>
[01:07.40] <Growing old disgracefully>
[01:10.20] <Still cracking jokes I shouldn't tell>
[01:14.08] <Still staying up a little too late>
[01:16.64] <Still giving common sense pure hell>
[01:20.46] <Some folks settle into wisdom>
[01:23.70] <I keep wandering accidentally>
[01:26.66] <Growing old disgracefully and having a great time doing it>
[01:52.58] <Bought a shirt too loud for my age, at least that's what my daughter said>
[01:59.06] <I wore it anyway to town and got more compliments instead>
[02:05.84] <The mirror says, "Act your age.">
[02:08.64] <The heart says, "That sounds boring.">
[02:11.86] <So we compromise once in a while and>
[02:14.94] <ignore each other every morning>
[02:18.02] <Growing old disgracefully>
[02:20.82] <Still dancing when the music plays>
[02:24.02] <Still telling stories that get longer every time they're told these>
[02:29.88] <days. The body's making suggestions, but I ignore them frequently>
[02:37.24] <Growing old disgracefully>
[02:42.32] <and somehow surviving beautifully>
[02:47.10] <I've earned every wrinkle I carry, every scar and every gray hair, too>
[02:53.46] <If getting older means acting proper, I might have a thing or two to refuse>
[03:02.86] <Growing old disgracefully with a smile I can't get rid of>
[03:09.22] <Laughing at things that used to worry me and holding tighter to what I love>
[03:15.86] <The years keep stacking higher, but they haven't tamed me completely>
[03:22.04] <Growing old disgracefully and I wouldn't have it any other way>
[03:36.53] <At my age, embarrassing yourself counts as>
[03:42.58] <cardio>